# Copy to .env (or set these in your host's environment) — all optional except the
# Upstox token, which Option Apex's dials need.
#
# api/.env is loaded automatically by every npm script here (--env-file-if-exists), and is
# gitignored. A clone with no .env still runs; only the Upstox-backed dials go quiet.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstox — serves EVERYTHING live: equity quotes, option chains, candles, open interest.
#
# Use an ANALYTICS TOKEN, not the ordinary OAuth access token:
#   * Analytics Token — read-only, generated once, valid ONE YEAR.
#   * Access token    — expires DAILY at 03:30 IST, so the dials would go dark each morning.
#
# Generate one at https://account.upstox.com/developer/apps -> Analytics tab -> Generate
# Token -> Confirm -> copy. Only one is active per account: generating a new one revokes
# the old, so if the dials start reporting 401, that is usually why.
UPSTOX_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# How long to wait on Upstox before giving up, ms. Default 8000.
UPSTOX_TIMEOUT_MS=8000

# Extra attempts after the first, for a timeout or a dropped socket. GETs only, so a
# repeat is safe, and the retry gets a 1.5x longer deadline than the attempt before it.
# Default 1. Set to 0 to disable retrying.
UPSTOX_RETRIES=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phone alerts (Telegram)
#
# Sends the pullback scanner's confirmed entries to your phone, during market hours
# only. Empty = no phone alerts; everything else in the app is unaffected.
#
# Setup, about two minutes:
#   1. In Telegram, message @BotFather -> /newbot -> pick a name -> it replies with a
#      token like 8123456789:AAF... -> paste it below.
#   2. Message your new bot anything at all (it cannot message you until you do).
#   3. Open https://api.telegram.org/bot<YOUR_TOKEN>/getUpdates and copy the numeric
#      "chat":{"id":...} -> paste it below.
#   4. Restart the API, then: curl -X POST http://localhost:4100/pullback/alerts/test
#
# These live here rather than in the scanner config because GET /pullback/config is
# served over HTTP — a bot token in there would be readable by anything that can reach
# the API, and a leaked token lets a stranger post trade instructions into your chat.
#
# WHAT gets sent (kinds, confidence floor) is configuration, not environment:
# GET/PUT /pullback/config -> alerts.push. Defaults to confirmed entries, Strong+.
PULLBACK_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
PULLBACK_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# Where the Bot API lives. Leave EMPTY unless api.telegram.org is blocked on your network.
#
# Many Indian ISPs filter Telegram by TLS SNI, and the symptom is confusing because nothing
# looks broken: DNS resolves, the TCP connection to api.telegram.org:443 completes, and the
# connection is then reset the instant the TLS handshake names that hostname. Node reports
# only "fetch failed", which reads like a credentials problem and is not one — the same IP
# with any other SNI connects fine, and web.telegram.org loads from the same machine. Ports
# 80, 88 and 8443 are no help either.
#
# The fix is to send through a host that is not on the blocklist. tools/telegram-mirror.worker.js
# is a Cloudflare Worker that forwards Bot API calls unchanged — free, ~5 minutes to deploy, and
# it must go in YOUR OWN Cloudflare account because the bot token passes through it.
#
# Check it worked: GET /pullback/status -> alerts.telegram.reachable = true, usingMirror = true.
#
# PULLBACK_TELEGRAM_API_BASE=https://tg-mirror.your-subdomain.workers.dev

# Discord, sent IN ADDITION to Telegram when both are set. Two independent channels
# means one can fail silently without costing you the alert — which is the failure
# mode that matters, since a channel that has quietly stopped looks exactly like a
# quiet market.
#
# Setup, about one minute:
#   1. Discord -> your server -> Edit Channel -> Integrations -> Webhooks
#      -> New Webhook -> Copy Webhook URL.
#      (No server? Press + on the left rail -> Create My Own -> it takes ten seconds.)
#   2. Paste it below and restart the API.
#   3. On your phone: long-press the channel -> Notifications -> All Messages,
#      or the alert will arrive silently and defeat the purpose.
#
# The URL is a credential — anyone holding it can post into that channel as you.
PULLBACK_DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R.Factor baseline — trailing sessions used as each stock's "normal" range.
# Built from Upstox daily candles, cached under api/.cache. Default 50.
RVOL_WINDOW=50

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Momentum Scanner
#
# The scanner's background jobs: a scan every 30s while the market is open, and a
# ~416-request baseline build once a day at 08:00 IST. Set to `off` to mount the API
# without them — worth doing on a second replica, since two processes both scanning
# spend the same token's request budget twice for one board.
#
# Everything else about the scanner (weights, thresholds, shortlist size, refresh
# intervals) is configuration, not environment: GET/PUT /momentum/config, or edit
# api/.cache/momentum/config.json. See api/src/momentum/config/defaults.ts.
MOMENTUM_SCHEDULER=on

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database (OPTIONAL — leave empty and everything keeps using api/.cache JSON files)
#
# Backs the three things that are genuinely worth querying across:
#   app_config        both scanner configs, versioned, so a board can say which model scored it
#   momentum_history  one row per symbol per session — the IV series Upstox does not publish,
#                     and which therefore exists nowhere but here
#   pullback_signal   every fired signal with its outcome — win rate by symbol, timeframe, hour
#
# Everything else stays on disk ON PURPOSE. The EMA seed (17.6 MB, read whole once a day), the
# volume baseline, the instrument master and the two boards are blobs with no query in them,
# and the boards are rewritten every 15 and 30 seconds — as inserts that is gigabytes a day to
# store something superseded seconds later. See api/src/db/wire.ts.
#
# Setup, about five minutes:
#   1. https://console.neon.tech -> sign up (no card) -> Create project.
#      Pick the region nearest you — Singapore (ap-southeast-1) for IST.
#   2. Copy the POOLED connection string (the host contains "-pooler") and paste it below.
#   3. cd api && npm run db:migrate     <- creates the tables and lifts existing .cache data in
#   4. Restart the API. Check it: curl http://localhost:4100/health -> db.connected = true
#
# A database that is set but unreachable is NOT fatal: the API logs it and carries on with the
# file store, because a trading board must not fail to start over an analytics table.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxx-pooler.ap-southeast-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# Connections held open. Default 5 — this is one process with one scheduler, not a web farm.
# DATABASE_POOL_MAX=5

# Only for a self-hosted Postgres with a self-signed certificate. Neon, Supabase and Aiven all
# present certificates from public CAs, so setting this against them just turns off the check
# that the host receiving your credential is the host you meant.
# DATABASE_SSL_INSECURE=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API port. Default 4100.
PORT=4100
